      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In the 1950s, massive land reclamation of Table Bay created the Cape Town foreshore, causing Woodstock beach to disappear and shifting the suburb from seaside resort to industrial.",
